---
/**
 * Hero. Single column, left aligned.
 *
 * The page opens on what the crate decides rather than on what it contains.
 * A reader who already knows what a quantum causal model is wants to know
 * whether this one checks the Markov condition or assumes it, and that answer
 * is the first concrete thing on the page.
 *
 * The dependency line is a git dependency because the crate carries
 * `publish = false`. Quoting CARGO_DEP keeps that fact in one file.
 */
import { Code } from 'astro:components';
import { rustDark, rustLight } from '../../../shiki-rust-themes.mjs';
import { CARGO_DEP, MSRV } from '../../consts';

const SHIKI = { light: rustLight, dark: rustDark };

const dep = `[dependencies]
${CARGO_DEP}`;
---
<section class="hero">
  <div class="hero-inner">
    <p class="eyebrow">DeepCausality · Quantum</p>
    <h1>Quantum causal models</h1>

    <p class="tagline">A causal graph whose factors are quantum channels.</p>

    <p class="sub">
      Each node carries a Choi–Jamiołkowski operator; the whole model is their
      product. Not every product is a legal model, and this crate decides which
      ones are at the freeze boundary, before a single step runs.
    </p>

    <Code code={dep} lang="toml" themes={SHIKI} />

    <p class="run-note">
      The crate is unpublished, so a git dependency is the only way to take it.
      The default build compiles the verifiable path and the causal-model slice;
      it pulls in no network and no async dependency at any feature setting.
      Rust {MSRV} or newer.
    </p>

    <div class="cta-row">
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/qcm/">
        Read the model
        <span class="btn-ico" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
      </a>
      <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/formalization/">
        See what is proved
      </a>
    </div>

    <p class="proof">
      Two factors declared on the same Hilbert leg. Diagonal ones commute, and
      the graph freezes with a recorded margin of <strong>0.000e0</strong>. Swap
      in <strong>σx</strong> against <strong>σz</strong> and the freeze aborts,
      names nodes 0 and 1 as the offending pair, and rolls the graph back:
      <code>is_frozen()</code> reports false.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .hero { padding: var(--space-8) var(--space-4) var(--space-7); }
  @media (min-width: 720px) { .hero { padding: var(--space-9) var(--space-5) var(--space-8); } }

  .hero-inner { max-width: var(--w-panel); margin: 0 auto; }

  h1 {
    font-size: clamp(2.25rem, 5vw + 0.5rem, 3.5rem);
    line-height: var(--lh-display);
    letter-spacing: var(--ls-display);
    margin: var(--space-3) 0 var(--space-4);
    max-width: 18ch;
  }
  .tagline {
    font-size: var(--t-h3);
    line-height: var(--lh-h3);
    color: var(--fg-0);
    max-width: var(--measure-lede);
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-4);
  }
  .sub {
    color: var(--fg-1);
    max-width: var(--measure-lede);
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-6);
  }

  .run-note {
    color: var(--fg-1);
    font-size: var(--t-body-sm);
    max-width: var(--measure);
    margin: var(--space-3) 0 var(--space-6);
  }

  .cta-row { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: var(--space-3); margin-bottom: var(--space-6); }
  .btn {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--space-2);
    height: 44px;
    padding: 0 var(--space-5);
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    border: 1px solid transparent;
    font-size: var(--t-body-sm);
    font-weight: var(--fw-heading);
    border-bottom: 1px solid transparent;
    transition: transform var(--dur-fast) var(--ease-out),
                background-color var(--dur-fast) var(--ease-out),
                border-color var(--dur-fast) var(--ease-out),
                color var(--dur-fast) var(--ease-out);
  }
  .btn:active { transform: translateY(1px); }
  .btn-primary { background: var(--accent); color: var(--accent-ink); }
  .btn-primary:hover {
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 90%, white);
    border-color: transparent;
    border-bottom-color: transparent;
  }
  .btn-ico { transition: transform var(--dur-fast) var(--ease-out); }
  .btn-primary:hover .btn-ico { transform: translateX(2px); }
  .btn-ghost { color: var(--fg-0); border-color: var(--line-2); }
  .btn-ghost:hover {
    border-color: var(--fg-2);
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 5%, transparent);
    border-bottom-color: var(--fg-2);
  }

  .proof {
    color: var(--fg-1);
    font-size: var(--t-body-sm);
    max-width: var(--measure);
    margin: 0;
    padding-left: var(--space-4);
    border-left: 2px solid var(--accent);
  }
  .proof strong { color: var(--fg-0); }
</style>
